sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch15-06> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The shape of an egg, as an extensible membrane filled with incompressible fluid under external pressure, obeys p_n + T(1/r + 1/r′) = P (external normal pressure plus membrane tension times total curvature equals internal pressure), which Thompson calls the equation of all eggs.";
    dc:type "mathematical-law";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Egg form obeys p_n + T(1/r + 1/r′) = P, the equation of all eggs";
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "p_n + T/r + T'/r' = P; with equal tensions p_n + T(1/r + 1/r') = P";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XV, “On the Shapes of Eggs, and of Certain Other Hollow Structures”; topic “Equation of the egg”. Scope: all hard-shelled and membrane-bound eggs"
}
